# 0058-iop-heap-reuse-and-refusal-report: the IOP heap reuses freed space, and a refused request is reported
#
# What it does: (1) IopMemory::allocate places a request in the first gap that fits, searching from HeapBase (before: from a cursor
# that only moved up, so freed space was never offered again); maxFreeMemory() answers the largest gap (before: limit minus cursor);
# totalFreeMemory() is new. (2) A refused request (size, alignment, fixed address, largest gap, total free) is written to stderr as
# "[ps2xIOP] heap request refused ...": the first four of each size, then every hundredth. Before, the effects driver died of a
# silent zero (journal 011). The heap base stays where patch 0057 put it; a fixed-address request behaves as before.
# Who asked is not printed (not cheap to know in this layer; a gdb backtrace on IopMemory::allocate gives it).
# Verified: tests/runtime/iop_heap_reuse_test fails (12 checks) without this patch and passes with it; iop_heap_capacity_test passes in both.
#
diff --git a/ps2xIOP/src/emulator/core/iop_memory.cpp b/ps2xIOP/src/emulator/core/iop_memory.cpp
index 7fb36d9..c59fdce 100644
--- a/ps2xIOP/src/emulator/core/iop_memory.cpp
